    "html": "<p>In a Compton scattering experiment a photon of wavelength <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda_{0}\"></span> and frequency <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"f_{0}\"></span> interacts with an electron.</p>\n<p>After the interaction the wavelength and frequency of the photon are <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"f\"></span>.</p>\n<p>What are <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\lambda}{\\lambda_{0}}\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\lambda\\times f}{\\lambda_{0}\\times f_{0}}\"></span>?<br/><br/></p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>[1]</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">Option A is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"B\">Option B is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"C\">Option C is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"D\">Option D is shown in the figure above.</li></ol>"
